      "title": "Temporary authority is specific",
      "narration": "In this scenario, an agency owner dies and an eligible relative needs to help preserve the business. Maryland may issue a temporary producer license without the usual examination to specified otherwise-qualified relatives, representatives or employees connected to a deceased or disabled producer. It is not automatic inheritance of a license. The person applies, pays the fee and obtains the temporary license and any required appointment before acting. The Commissioner must issue or refuse it in writing within thirty days of receiving the application. This Maryland temporary license expires fifteen months after its effective date.",
